--TEST--
A signing literal that leaves `until` out is refused at the call, because a signature's lifetime is a required key whose `null` is the forever spelling — `rule:core-api/a-lifetime-is-written`, E0402
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The boundary the rule exists for. `{keys: $ring, until: null}` compiles and
// signs a link that never expires; this literal says nothing about a lifetime
// at all, and that is the spelling the language does not have. A permanent
// signed link is a permanent bearer credential — written into browser history,
// `Referer` headers, proxy logs and chat unfurls — so "forever" is something a
// person types rather than something a missing key chooses.
//
// It is a *shape* and not an options bag for exactly this: `rule:core-api/shape-rules` R2 makes
// every member of a bag optional, so a bag could not have refused anything here.
secret bytes $key = Core\Crypto::generateKey();
array<secret bytes> $ring = [$key];

Core\Signature::sign(["doc" => "7"], {keys: $ring});

// And at the door whose payload is derived rather than written, because one
// shape serves every door onto `rule:core-api/signing-is-over-a-payload`: a
// lifetime that were required at the general member and optional at the URL
// is exactly the hole the shared const exists to make unspellable.
Core\Uri::parse("https://example.test/a")->sign({keys: $ring});
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0402]: this member requires the shape key `until`
   --> %s:14:38
   |
14 | Core\Signature::sign(["doc" => "7"], {keys: $ring});
   |                                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `until` is not given
   = help: the keys this member requires are: keys, until

error[E0402]: this member requires the shape key `until`
   --> %s:20:49
   |
20 | Core\Uri::parse("https://example.test/a")->sign({keys: $ring});
   |                                                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `until` is not given
   = help: the keys this member requires are: keys, until

error: aborting due to 2 errors
